t  times but it's pretty dire straits at  this point so what does that mean for us  will we be fined if we go outside yeah I  mean we have seen past precedent for it  in San Francisco you can already receive  a  if you are going out for a nonessential  reason in Italy we've seen that you had  to carry around actually a piece of  paper explaining your reason for being  outdoors South Korea has also  implemented fines I think ultimately  especially in the u.s. they're trying to  exercise compassion with those types of  rules that they do implement them I  understand that this is difficult time  that people do want to have some fresh  air but ultimately this is a necessary  measure to sort of protect the public  safety at large now this is a question  that I feel like many in my circle want  to know the answer to but do sometimes  have some countries implemented these  rules but with exceptions for people  with dogs or pets yeah there are  exceptions for people with dogs or pets  we actually know that pets can't  contract the virus but we understand  that they need to be outdoors to sort of  do their business so that's one of the  reasons why you know pet owners would  have a legitimate excuse for being  outdoors they should still make sure to  practice the safe distancing of six feet  from another person and it should only  be just a reason to walk your dog and  get back inside if your city has already  implemented one of those self isolating  policies Sariah as a country when did we  start taking this seriously  so I just spoke to a laboratory  researcher in Seattle who actually  developed his labs on Kovach 19 tests so  he was telling me that the u.s. actually  started taking this pandemic now  seriously about two to three days ago  and that was when we started  implementing some of those stricter  social isolation measures it was  actually also when we realized that we  were sort of in the same boat as China  and Italy in terms of our death count of  the way that cases have risen probably  should have been a bit more proactive  with our social distancing measures  because we do know that that's one of  the most effective ways of containing  this virus and the fact that we've  waited until now means that we might  have to resort to more drastic measures  in the future  [Music]  [Music]
 

